  "result": "JWT `exp` field = Unix seconds. `Date.now()` = milliseconds.\n\n**Bug:** comparison off by 1000x \u2014 token expired in 2024 looks valid until year 33658.\n\n**Fix:**\n\n```js\n// Wrong\nif (Date.now() > payload.exp) { ... }\n\n// Correct\nif (Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000) > payload.exp) { ... }\n// or\nif (Date.now() > payload.exp * 1000) { ... }\n```\n\nPick one form, stay consistent. Also add clock skew buffer if needed:\n\n```js\nconst CLOCK_SKEW_SECONDS = 30;\nif (Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000) > payload.exp + CLOCK_SKEW_SECONDS) {\n  throw new Error('Token expired');\n}\n```",
